+  `redmine.secret_key_base` initializer of `config/application.rb`) keeps the
+  `secret_key_base` Rails 7.0 used: Rails 7.2 no longer reads
+  `config/secrets.yml` and prefers `config.secret_key_base` to
+  `ENV['SECRET_KEY_BASE']` and the credentials.
+* Overrides introduced: `run_commit_callbacks_on_first_saved_instances_in_transaction = true`,
+  `run_after_transaction_callbacks_in_order_defined = false`,
+  `default_column_serializer = YAML`, `yjit = false`,
+  `enqueue_after_transaction_commit = :never` (removed in this release), see
+  the tables above. Adopted then: the HTML5 sanitizer and test parser,
+  SQLite strict strings, `add_autoload_paths_to_load_path = false`,
+  `postgresql_adapter_decode_dates`, `raise_on_invalid_cache_expiration_time`,
+  `validate_migration_timestamps`, `precompile_filter_parameters`,
+  `raise_on_assign_to_attr_readonly`, `generate_secure_token_on`,
+  `before_committed_on_all_records`, `belongs_to_required_validates_foreign_key`,
